<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mount Tambora</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mount Tambora is a volcano on the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumbawa">Sumbawa</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. Its eruption in April 1815, the largest in recorded history, destroyed the kingdoms of Tambora and Pekat and killed tens of thousands of people on Sumbawa and nearby islands. The ash it threw into the atmosphere caused the 'year without a summer' of 1816 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mount-tambora.jpg" alt="Mount Tambora" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This image was taken by the NASA Expedition 20 crew. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mount_Tambora_Volcano,_Sumbawa_Island,_Indonesia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
